    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d242">

                <pb facs="0368" n="283" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg283"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">814.51/309: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Thurston</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-11-03T15:00:00-06:36"><hi rendition="#italic">November 3,
                                1919, 3 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received
                            November 5, 9.15 a.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Strictly confidential. Department’s October 25, 7 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >6</hi>] p.m., my October 30, noon.<anchor n="12" xml:id="d242-f1"/> President
                    Cabrera informed me during an interview this morning that Professor Kemmerer’s
                    report was being translated, but he did not intimate that it would be made
                    public.</p>
                <pb facs="0369" n="284" xml:id="pg284"/>
                <p>He further stated that he would instruct Minister Mendez to request the
                    Department to make such use of this report as might appear desirable.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thurston</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d242-f1" n="12" xml:id="d242-f1-content">
                <p>Latter not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
